# 2. ABSTRACT

The Smart Parking System using Ultrasonic Sensors is an embedded system designed to monitor parking slot availability in real time. The system uses four HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensors with an Arduino UNO to detect whether individual parking slots are free or occupied based on measured distance. The available slot count is displayed on a 16×2 I2C LCD, while LED and buzzer indicators provide parking status and full-capacity alerts.

The prototype was implemented and tested virtually using Wokwi. Different sensor-distance conditions were simulated to represent vehicles entering and leaving parking slots. The system successfully identified free and occupied slots, calculated available spaces, displayed the parking status, and activated the parking-full alert when all slots were occupied.

The project demonstrates important embedded-system concepts including GPIO interfacing, sensor integration, distance measurement, threshold-based decision making, real-time status monitoring, output control, serial communication, and embedded C/C++ programming.

